---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import ScreenshotSlot from '../../components/ScreenshotSlot.astro';
import GamingModes from '../../components/GamingModes.astro';
import WorkshopLinks from '../../components/WorkshopLinks.astro';
import art from '../../assets/projects/ai-gaming.png';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<SiteLayout title="AI Gaming" description="The paused AI Gaming Development source offers player-confirmed Ollama Local advice. In-game behavior remains unverified." path="ai-gaming/" active="mods">
	<section class="hero page-wrap">
		<div class="hero-copy">
			<p class="eyebrow">Development paused · historical preview 0.4.0</p>
			<h1>AI Gaming</h1>
			<p class="hero-lead">The 0.4.0 Development source offers Ollama Local advice through a Windows x64 Companion. Review the city data and installed-content identifiers, write a question and confirm each complete request. Replies are advice only; this preview does not control the simulation.</p>
			<div class="status-strip"><span class="tag">Ollama Local</span><span class="tag">Confirm every request</span><span class="tag">Game runtime unverified</span><span class="tag">English · 繁體中文</span></div>
			<WorkshopLinks mod="ai-gaming" />
		</div>
		<figure class="hero-art"><Image src={art} alt="AI Gaming artwork" widths={[560, 720]} sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 45vw" format="webp" quality={78} loading="eager" /><figcaption class="art-note">Project artwork · not a gameplay screenshot</figcaption></figure>
	</section>

	<nav class="subnav page-wrap" aria-label="AI Gaming guide"><a href={base + 'wiki/ai-gaming/overview/'}>Guide</a><a href={base + 'wiki/project/roadmap/'}>Roadmap</a></nav>

	<section class="section soft">
		<div class="page-wrap columns">
			<div class="text-stack">
				<p class="eyebrow">Earlier Development source</p>
				<h2>Review every request before confirming it.</h2>
				<p>The settings page in <a href="https://github.com/KingsleyHK0323/Cities_Skylines_1_Modpack/blob/e7de649f58c775f0692ef74d62eed351cf2d6607/Source/LocalAiRequestController.cs">Development source e7de649</a> offers six basic fields: game date, population, funds, residential demand, commercial demand and workplace demand. It also offers four data groups: utilities, built zoned buildings, traffic and public transport, and city service status. All six fields and four groups start selected and can be deselected.</p>
				<p>Identifiers for DLC, creator packs and radio stations that the game reports as installed and available are added automatically, without a separate selection control. The preview shows the data, model name and question before each confirmation.</p>
				<p>The separate city-summary command remains available; on request it writes the game date, population, funds, residential demand, commercial demand and workplace demand to the local game log.</p>
				<p>Each request needs a separate confirmation. The response is displayed as advice only; it is not interpreted as a game action. The source has no cloud-provider adapter or API-key entry.</p>
				<p>After each confirmation, AI Gaming sends the previewed data, model name and question through the local Companion to Ollama on this PC. Ollama may route inference to a cloud service depending on its own configuration, which the mod cannot inspect. Do not include city names, account information, secrets or personal data in the free-text question.</p>
				{false && (
				<p lang="en"><strong>Distribution update, 3 November 2026:</strong> AI Gaming remains paused and is not among the AI Improve and Automated Public Transport Planning artifact-branch candidates. The package guidance below is historical and does not establish current availability or game acceptance.</p>
				)}
				<p lang="en"><strong>Development status:</strong> AI Gaming remains paused. If Dev Manager's Windows Setup.exe has been published, check <a href="https://github.com/KingsleyHK0323/Cities_Skylines_1_Modpack/releases">GitHub Releases</a>. The planned app is intended to show verified module builds when available; availability varies by module. Earlier package guidance is historical and does not establish current availability or game acceptance.</p>
				<!-- Notice wording: OpenAI-Codex_distribution_components. -->
				<p class="section-intro" lang="en">AI Gaming remains paused. In-game behavior and Ollama requests remain unverified. Back up saves and use a separate test city.</p>
				<details>
					<summary lang="en">Historical package guidance - not a current download</summary>
				<p class="section-intro"><strong>Development build status:</strong> Development is paused. An earlier package used separate DLL and Windows x64 Companion assets; current public availability is unverified. If matching official assets are available, use both files from the same release: the DLL requires the exact Companion hash. Publication and file checks do not establish successful Cities: Skylines gameplay or Ollama requests; both remain unverified. Back up saves and test in a separate city.</p>
				</details>
			</div>
			<div class="screenshot-stack">
				<ScreenshotSlot title="Ollama request preview" description="The selected city data, automatically added installed-content identifiers, model name, question and separate confirmation control." />
				<ScreenshotSlot title="Advice response" description="The model response displayed as advice, without changing the simulation." />
				<ScreenshotSlot title="City summary in the log" description="The separate manual summary with the game date, population, funds and residential, commercial and workplace demand." />
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="interactive-section"><div class="page-wrap"><p class="section-label">The idea · three ways to play</p><h2>How you and the AI could share a city.</h2><GamingModes locale="en" /></div></section>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="page-wrap">
			<p class="eyebrow">Roadmap and safeguards</p>
			<h2>You stay in control.</h2>
			<div class="roadmap"><article><strong>1 · Observe</strong><p>Selected aggregate city data is available in the Development source.</p></article><article><strong>2 · Suggest</strong><p>Player-confirmed Ollama Local advice is implemented in the historical Development source; game runtime remains unverified.</p></article><article><strong>3 · Act, with permission</strong><p>Game actions are not implemented and remain planned.</p></article></div>
			<p class="section-intro">The Development source detects providers and reads interop manifests. Calling capabilities from other Modpack mods and interoperability in game have not been established. Cloud-provider adapters and gameplay actions are not implemented.</p>
			<a class="text-link" href={base + 'wiki/project/roadmap/'}>Full roadmap →</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</SiteLayout>
